#%PAM-1.0

# A VNC login is the phone's PIN coming in over a network, where nobody watches: every password
# goes through plinius-pinguard with its own counter for network logins. That counter always
# counts, also when the wait for PINs at the phone is off, and failed tries here don't lock the
# phone itself. No fallback to pam_unix: without the daemon nobody logs in over VNC.
auth    required pam_plinius_pinguard.so network
account required pam_unix.so
